%% plays.glp --- the GKK mini-app activated as the super-app activates it (GSG paper, Section 2, "Activation and joining"): by run/3, under the type identity of its entry miniapp/4, with its grants; and, for three executions, with the two ends of a root channel handed to each two of them as their conversation, the play standing in for the social graph, as ../gsg/plays.glp does.  The persons are scripted (person.glp), each under its role, and the play returns their screens.  A run does not end --- the agent's request question stays open and the person channel never closes --- so once each agent has taken its own transactions until none holds and no trigger is left, the run suspends, and a play's result is read off a partial stream.

imported procedure person#miniapp_person(Key?, Constant?, Channel(PersonOut(Drawn), PersonIn(Drawn))?, Stream(Seen)).

%% play_keys(A, B, C): alice, bob and carol, a conversation between alice's execution and bob's, one between alice's and carol's, and one between bob's and carol's, which the social graph would open between friends and which carries the agents' ihellos.  Each establishes their identity (GKK:1, Identity); alice and bob ask to know each other, and so do alice and carol; alice asks to come to know bob, and he answers yes, after which each knows the other (GKK:2, Acquaintance, an act of both); alice and carol come to know each other likewise; and alice, who knows bob and carol, introduces carol to bob, he answers yes, and he then knows carol (GKK:3, Introduction, an act of alice and bob).  At the commit alice's agent introduces carol's agent and bob's to each other, intro(carol) to bob and intro(bob) to carol: her role requires knows(c), c an agent variable bound to carol, and bob's role gains knows(c), so the introduction rule gives alice the pair {bob, carol} (vGLP 613ee8d, Definition "Introduction Rule, Introduce Peers"; Section 5.4, "Act schemas as local specifications": "under GKK:3 Alice introduces Carol and Bob").  Bob's agent and carol's then exchange ihellos and know each other, and bob asks to come to know carol, she answers yes, and each knows the other.  The acts up to the introduction are those of the screens of GKK's app (screens/).
exported procedure play_keys(Stream(Seen), Stream(Seen), Stream(Seen)).
play_keys(A?, B?, C?) :-
    self_module(M),
    find_type(miniapp/4, T),
    run(miniapp(alice, ch(GA?, DA), ch([conversation(bob, ch(BA?, AB)), conversation(carol, ch(CA?, AC))], _), []), T?, M?),
    person # miniapp_person(alice, alice, ch(DA?, GA), A),
    run(miniapp(bob, ch(GB?, DB), ch([conversation(alice, ch(AB?, BA)), conversation(carol, ch(CB?, BC))], _), []), T?, M?),
    person # miniapp_person(bob, bob, ch(DB?, GB), B),
    run(miniapp(carol, ch(GC?, DC), ch([conversation(alice, ch(AC?, CA)), conversation(bob, ch(BC?, CB))], _), []), T?, M?),
    person # miniapp_person(carol, carol, ch(DC?, GC), C).
